(;GM[1]FF[4]CA[UTF-8]SZ[19]KM[7.5]RU[Chinese]EV[Google DeepMind Challenge Match, game 2]DT[2016-03-10]PC[Four Seasons Hotel, Seoul]PB[AlphaGo]PW[Lee Sedol]WR[9p]RE[B+R]SO[Move list from Andries Brouwer's game archive, https://homepages.cwi.nl/~aeb/go/games/games/AlphaGo/LeeSedol/2.sgf, checked 2026-09-14 against Wikipedia, "AlphaGo versus Lee Sedol" (AlphaGo Black, B+R, 211 moves, move 37 by Black at P10). Comments are Go Master's own.]C[Game 2 of the 2016 match. AlphaGo (Black) against Lee Sedol 9p (White). Chinese rules, komi 7.5. A modern opening: 4-4 and 3-4 points, then approaches, with the sides and centre left open. Use the arrows or ← → to step through.]
;B[pd]C[Q16, the 4-4 point (hoshi). It sits on a star point, takes the corner loosely and looks along both sides.];W[dp]C[D4, another 4-4 point, in the opposite corner.];B[cd]C[C16: a 3-4 point in a third corner.];W[qp]C[R4: a 3-4 point in the fourth. Four corners in four moves.];B[op]C[P4: Black approaches White's 3-4 stone at R4 from the side where it faces the open board.];W[oq]C[P3, an attachment underneath — one of the standard answers to the approach.];B[nq]C[O3, the hane.];W[pq]C[Q3: White connects and takes the corner.];B[cn]C[C6: Black leaves the right side for the moment and approaches D4.];W[fq]C[F3: White answers the approach with a knight's move along the bottom.]
;B[mp]C[N4: Black returns to the right and extends solidly from P4 — a stone that will be short of liberties otherwise.];W[qn]C[R6: White extends up the right side from the corner.];B[ic]C[J17: a wide extension along the top between C16 and Q16 — a framework, not territory yet.];W[dj]C[D10: White extends along the left, also a framework.];B[po]C[Q5, pressing on the corner.];W[qo]C[R5: White answers.];B[cp]C[C4: Black attaches to the 4-4 stone from below, starting a sequence in the corner.];W[cq];B[bq];W[co]
;B[bp];W[bo];B[do];W[bn];B[dq];W[ep];B[dr];W[cm];B[jp];W[cg]
;B[ed];W[qf];B[qe];W[pf];B[nd];W[pi];B[oj]C[Move 37, the shoulder hit at P10 on the fifth line, is the move commentators called the most creative of the match — one that a professional would not have considered. The sequence to here is the opening; the game was decided in the fights that followed. AlphaGo won by resignation after 211 moves.];W[oi];B[nj];W[mh]
